CORE
main.cpp
--cpp14
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ void\(\) performs no initialization: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
cannot zero-initialize
--
N5008 [expr.type.conv]/2: "if the type is cv void and the initializer is ()
or {} (after pack expansion, if any), the expression is a prvalue of type
void that performs no initialization".  The front end value-initialized the
operand-less functional cast and rejected `void()' with "cannot
zero-initialize 'void'" (and `void{}' through the constructor-call path),
(the braced `void{}' of N5008 is accepted by g++ 13 but not yet by
clang++ 18, so this test uses the parenthesized form only), e.g. libc++'s `return void();' in __get_comp_type (KNOWNBUG
cpp20_compare_three_way_pointers_libcxx).  Fixed in round 163b.
